7: \nL8: [Submitted on 18 Nov 1999]\nL9: # Title:On Stable Sector in Supermembrane Matrix Model\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†I.Ya. Aref'eva , cite6†A.S. Koshelev , cite7†P.B. Medvedev L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled On Stable Sector in Supermembrane Matrix Model, by I.Ya. Aref'eva and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract: We study the spectrum of SU(2) x SO(2) matrix supersymmetric quantum mechanics. We use angular coordinates that allow us to find an explicit solution of the Gauss law constraints and single out the quantum number n (the Lorentz angular momentum). Energy levels are four-fold degenerate with respect to n and are labeled by n_q, the largest n in a quartet. The Schrödinger equation is reduced to two different systems of two-dimensional partial differential equations.\nL17: The choice of a system is governed by n_q. We present the asymptotic solutions for the systems deriving thereby the asymptotic formula for the spectrum. Odd n_q are forbidden, for even n_q the spectrum has a continuous part as well as a discrete one, meanwhile for half-integer n_q the spectrum is purely discrete. Taking half-integer n_q one can cure the model from instability caused by the presence of continuous spectrum.\nL18: Comments:  | 29 pages, 5 figures\nL19: Subjects:  | High Energy Physics - Theory (hep-th)\nL20: Report number:  | SMI-5-99\nL21: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:hep-th/9911149 L22:    | (or cite11†arXiv:hep-th/9911149v1 for this version)\nL23:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.hep-th/9911149†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: Journal reference:  | Nucl.Phys. B579 (2000) 411-436\nL25: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | cite13†https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213%2800%2900205-4†doi.org DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Irina Arefeva [cite14†view email ]\nL29: [v1] Thu, 18 Nov 1999 23:22:21 UTC (49 KB)\nL30: \n